\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.2}Magnification Technique}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Raw measurements for the magnification experiment. We used the Vernier Caliper to measure either the height or the width, I think it was the width because the height of the image and of the object was very awkward to measure. We figured it wouldn't matter because the magnification relies about the size of the image not which parts to measure. The magnification should be collected if we measured the same parts. }}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:magnification}{{2}{4}{}{table.2}{}}
